At long last, my first priest ascension! And in Spork, no less!

Did I mention priests suck? The intrinsic b/u/c detection is the only
advantage over a comparable healer. No healing spells, the weakest
weapon skills in the game, a mediocre quest artifact, puny starting
stats, terrible HP growth, well, *you get the idea*.

This priest, in fact, played the early game healer-style and went for
the racket. I've gotten much, much better at this; the hard part of
the protection racket is knowing when *not* to do the racket. In my
mind, the requirements are:

1. At least 800 gold pieces
2. Early digging tool/wand from mines
3. Some method of teleportation for an emergency.
4. A large dog or cat.
5. Negative AC *before* the run start.

I found approximately 2000 gold pieces through raiding an (eel-less!)
vault and credit cloning my starting spellbooks, a wand of
teleportation on a dead hobbit, and a wand of digging lying on the
ground. And I found a +1 banded mail because priests always find stuff
like that. Sometimes, just sometimes, I like being a priest.

I was in business. I dug straight down to College town, and actually
credit-cloned some more at the bookstore. I also found a magic lamp in
the hardware store, heh heh. Saving the dig for later, hit the
oracles, got a water demon wish for 2 cursed scrolls of genocide.
Nurse-danced to 100 HP or so, solved Sokoban, returned to the mines
and grabbed the luckstone. As usual, chased a gray unicorn for luck.

Dug farther down, found a coaligned temple and made it my stash level.
Reversed genocided silver dragons, wished for the +2 Staff of
Aesculapius, and kicked some dragon butt. Got SDSM. With AC-19 before
SDSM, and around 150 HP, I was plenty ready for the castle.

Enchanting the Staff to +7 produced incredible results, easily
finishing the castle. The staff was my main weapon until the endgame,
when I accidentally polypiled it, possibly the single stupidest stupid
thing I've done in Nethack. Frustrated, I made ten or so +9 darts and
polypiled for a +9 mace and +9 spetum. I never used the nice poisoned
darts, since hey, EXP28 priest and magic missile = ass kicking, but
the +9 mace, together with a +6 ring of increase damage, worked well
enough for my purposes. It would have been nice to get a +9 staff
since I'd still get double strength damage (Spork mod), but oh well, a
cursed +9 staff would have done me no good.

Endgame AC was -39 or so, even with a bunch of burnt and rotted armor.
Helped a lot, since I had dug past the demon lords and didn't have the
50000000 or so gold pieces they desired. Also, mysterious force didn't
throw me back even *once*. WOW.

Things got dicey when I ran out of death wand charges, but since I
brought a *ton* of wands of teleportation, and jumping boots (I've
learned), genocided L and h, and genocided ; on the Plane of Water, it
was a decent run. Had a helm of opposite alignment, but since second
altar was neutral, decided to offer the amulet to my native deity.
Hey, he was nice enough to crown me on my first altar prayer, so he
deserves *some* loyalty.

